        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1777581874877",
            "name": "Classify Balance Inquiry Scope"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1777582178985"
          },
          "code": "FIN_GL_LLM_BALANCE_INQUIRY_SCOPE_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1777577031605",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1777577031606_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Objective\n\nClassify the user's current turn into one workflow path.\n\nYou only determine the scope path and whether the user explicitly asked to sort the balance result. Do not extract query details, do not rewrite the user request, do not decide tool calls, do not update state, and do not format a final answer.\n\n## Input\n\nThe current user message is: <USER_MESSAGE> {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} </USER_MESSAGE>\n\nChat History: <CHAT_HISTORY> {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}} </CHAT_HISTORY>\n\n## Scope Paths\n\nReturn exactly one scopeType:\n\n- new_query: The user asks for a new balance result or changes query-defining business scope.\n- breakdown: The user asks to add, remove, clear, replace, drill, expand, group, split, or show contributors for the active balance query's COA or period/time breakdown without changing query-defining business scope.\n- sort: The user only asks to sort/order the active balance result without changing query-defining business scope or breakdown state.\n- new_query_plus_breakdown: The user changes query-defining business scope and also asks to add, remove, clear, replace, drill, expand, group, split, or show contributors for a COA or period/time breakdown in the same turn.\n- out_of_scope: The user is not asking for balance retrieval, balance breakdown, or balance result sorting.\n- clarification_needed: The request is balance-related but cannot be classified safely from the provided context.\n\n## Classification Rules\n\nQuery-defining business scope includes:\n- accounting period or date range when used as a filter\n- currency or currency type\n- balance measure, such as period activity, beginning balance, ending balance, PTD, QTD, or YTD\n- comparison or variance request, including side by side or side-by-side balance or period comparison\n- COA segment filter values, such as company, account, cost center, department, intercompany, or product, when used as filters\n\nScope-changing filter rule:\n- Adding, changing, replacing, narrowing, broadening, or removing any filter condition is a query-defining business scope change.\n- A filter condition is any constraint that determines which balance rows or values should be retrieved, included, excluded, compared, aggregated, or returned.\n- Filters may target business dimensions such as company, account, cost center, department, product, period, currency, ledger, or balance measures such as period activity, ending balance, variance amount, and variance percentage.\n- Do not treat a request as presentation-only merely because the user says \"show rows\", \"only show\", \"filter\", \"where\", or \"with\"; if the condition controls which balance rows qualify, it is query-defining.\n- If the user adds or changes a filter condition while also requesting, preserving, or relying on an active COA or period/time breakdown, return `new_query_plus_breakdown`.\n- Return `breakdown` only when the user changes COA or period/time breakdown state and does not add, remove, or change any filter condition.\n\nMeasure filters and thresholds are filter conditions:\n- Numeric predicates, thresholds, ranges, equality, or ordering conditions on balance measures or computed balance result columns are query-defining filters.\n- This includes conditions on period activity, beginning balance, ending balance, PTD, QTD, YTD, balance amount, variance amount, variance percentage, change percentage, or displayed balance/result rows.\n- Treat phrases such as \"greater than\", \"more than\", \"over\", \"above\", \"at least\", \"less than\", \"under\", \"below\", \"at most\", \"between\", \"equals\", \"not equal\", \"top\", \"bottom\", and operators such as `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`, `=`, `!=` as predicates when applied to those measures.\n\nBreakdown intent includes:\n- break down\n- remove breakdown\n- clear breakdown\n- stop grouping by\n- no longer group by\n- only by\n- split\n- group by\n- drill down\n- expand\n- contributors\n- children\n- descendants\n- last descendants\n- direct children\n- immediate descendants\n- next level\n- one level under\n- leaf\n- detail\n- lowest level\n- by period\n- by accounting period\n- by time period\n- period-wise\n- by quarter\n- by month\n\nDo not classify a COA segment or period/time mention as a scope-changing filter when it is only used as a breakdown, grouping, drill, expansion, contributor, or detail dimension.\n\nSort routing:\n- If the user explicitly asks to sort/order the balance result, set sortRequired to true.\n- Do not change the main scope just because sort is mentioned.\n- Use scopeType sort only when sorting is the only requested change.\n\nUse clarification_needed sparingly. Prefer another scope path when the likely path is clear.\n\nUse out_of_scope for journals, subledgers, reports, setup/configuration, operational tasks, help/how-to questions, export, display formatting, column visibility, charting, summarization, or presentation-only requests that are not balance result sorting.\n- Do not classify a message as `out_of_scope` merely because it is phrased as a statement. If the turn is a declarative statement or fragment that mentions a balance/account balance, threshold, variance, comparison, sort, or breakdown, treat it as an implicit balance retrieval request unless it clearly asks for a non-balance task.\n\n## Out-of-Scope Categories\n\nWhen `scopeType` is `out_of_scope`, also return `out_of_scope_category`.\n\nUse one of:\n\n- MULTIPLE_FINANCIAL_OBJECTS: The same user question combines balances with another financial object/domain, such as journals, subledgers, suppliers, invoices, or journal sources.\n  Examples: What is the total cash balance and its contributing journal sources? Show account balance and related journal lines.\n\n- JOURNAL_SCOPE: The request is specifically for journal headers, journal lines, journal batches, journal sources, journal categories, postings, reversals, or journal activity rather than balance retrieval.\n\n- SUBLEDGER_SCOPE: The request is for subledger transactions, invoices, receipts, suppliers, customers, payments, or accounting distributions.\n\n- SETUP_OR_OPERATIONAL_TASK: The request asks to configure, create, update, approve, post, reverse, close, open, or perform an operational/setup task.\n\n- NON_BALANCE_SCOPE: The request is not a balance retrieval, balance breakdown, or balance result sorting request and does not fit the categories above.\n\nOnly classify as `MULTIPLE_FINANCIAL_OBJECTS` when multiple objects are requested in the same user question. A follow-up may refer to a different object and should be classified based on the current turn plus relevant chat history.\n\nFor non-out-of-scope paths, return `out_of_scope_category` as an empty string.\n\n## Examples\n\nUnless an example explicitly says otherwise, sortRequired is false.\n\n- \"Show period activity for cash in Mar-26\" -> new_query\n- \"Show balances for account 10000 sorted by period activity desc\" -> new_query with sortRequired true\n- \"Now for Apr-26\" -> new_query\n- \"Use USD instead\" -> new_query\n- \"Compare Mar-26 to Feb-26\" -> new_query\n- \"Refresh it\" -> new_query\n- \"Run that again\" -> new_query\n- \"Break that down by cost center\" -> breakdown\n- \"Breakdown by period\" -> breakdown\n- \"Break down by cost center sorted by period activity desc\" -> breakdown with sortRequired true\n- \"Sort by period activity desc\" -> sort with sortRequired true\n- \"Order it by ledger then account\" -> sort with sortRequired true\n- \"drill down by quarter\" -> breakdown\n- \"breakdown by 2025\" -> breakdown\n- \"expand Qtr2-25 to periods\" -> breakdown\n- \"Remove breakdown by period\" -> breakdown\n- \"Expand account 5000\" -> breakdown\n- \"Show descendants of account 5000\" -> breakdown\n- \"Show immediate descendants of company 100\" -> breakdown\n- \"Show company 100 by child companies\" -> breakdown\n- \"Show leaf accounts\" -> breakdown\n- \"Remove cost center breakdown\" -> breakdown\n- \"Clear the breakdown\" -> breakdown\n- \"Only break it down by account\" -> breakdown\n- \"For Apr-26, show revenue by company\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown\n- \"For Apr-26, show revenue by company sorted by ending balance\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown with sortRequired true\n- \"Show ending balance for expenses in USD by cost center\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown\n- \"For Apr-26, remove company breakdown\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown\n- \"Show cash balance for 2025 by period\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown\n- \"Show revenue for current year by quarter\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown\n- \"For Qtr1-26, broken down by period\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown\n- With an active Account leaf breakdown, \"show the rows with variance percentage > 50%\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown\n- \"Show rows where period activity is below 0 by company\" -> new_query_plus_breakdown\n- \"Show balances greater than 10000\" -> new_query\n- \"Show the journal lines for this account\" -> out_of_scope with JOURNAL_SCOPE\n- \"What is the total cash balance and its contributing journal sources?\" -> out_of_scope with MULTIPLE_FINANCIAL_OBJECTS\n- \"How do I post a journal?\" -> out_of_scope with SETUP_OR_OPERATIONAL_TASK\n\n## Output\n\nReturn JSON only. Do not wrap in Markdown. Do not include comments or extra fields.\njson\n{\"scopeType\":\"<scope>\", \"sortRequired\": false, \"reasoning\":\"<concise explanation of why path chosen>\", \"out_of_scope_category\":\"<category when scopeType is out_of_scope, otherwise empty string>\"}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"scopeType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"new_query\",\n        \"breakdown\",\n        \"sort\",\n        \"new_query_plus_breakdown\",\n        \"out_of_scope\",\n        \"clarification_needed\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"sortRequired\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"reasoning\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"maxLength\": 500\n    },\n    \"out_of_scope_category\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"\",\n        \"MULTIPLE_FINANCIAL_OBJECTS\",\n        \"JOURNAL_SCOPE\",\n        \"SUBLEDGER_SCOPE\",\n        \"SETUP_OR_OPERATIONAL_TASK\",\n        \"NON_BALANCE_SCOPE\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"scopeType\",\n    \"sortRequired\",\n    \"reasoning\",\n    \"out_of_scope_category\"\n  ],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
